1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,393
Reading the Signals.

2
00:00:01,393 --> 00:00:06,740
You've positioned the card. You've asked
the questions. Maybe you've handled some

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:12,153
resistance. Now you need to make a call:
is this prospect a fit for float, a Net-1

4
00:00:12,153 --> 00:00:16,765
close, or something that shouldn't go to
the underwriting team at all?

5
00:00:16,765 --> 00:00:18,948
Here are the signals that tell you.

6
00:00:18,948 --> 00:00:20,295
Financial Signals.

7
00:00:20,295 --> 00:00:26,276
First — personal credit cards funding the
ads. If the founder is swiping a personal

8
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:31,383
Amex to run Meta campaigns, the business
doesn't have its own financial

9
00:00:31,383 --> 00:00:34,738
infrastructure yet. Net-1 is the right
product.

10
00:00:34,738 --> 00:00:40,952
Second — burn exceeds revenue with short
runway. They raised five million dollars.

11
00:00:40,952 --> 00:00:46,706
You ask about cash and they say two
hundred thousand. That means they burned

12
00:00:46,706 --> 00:00:52,690
through $4.8 million. A company spending
more than it makes isn't automatically

13
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:58,827
disqualified — growth-stage brands burn
cash intentionally. But burn greater than

14
00:00:58,827 --> 00:01:04,735
revenue with less than six months of
runway is a sign that the Net1 may be the

15
00:01:04,735 --> 00:01:06,039
only option here.

16
00:01:06,039 --> 00:01:11,646
Any one of these signals means float is
off the table. That's not a dead deal —

17
00:01:11,646 --> 00:01:16,534
it's a Net-1 close until the company's
financial profile strengthens.

18
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:18,113
Industry signals.

19
00:01:18,113 --> 00:01:23,015
Revenue isn't the only predictor of
underwriting outcomes. For the same

20
00:01:23,015 --> 00:01:28,267
reason a 10-million-dollar supplement
brand get's approved for float while a

21
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:33,589
10-hundred-million-dollar auto parts
retailer gets denied. There are types of

22
00:01:33,589 --> 00:01:38,701
business models that may have trouble
getting approved for extended terms.

23
00:01:38,701 --> 00:01:40,312
Here's a four examples:

24
00:01:40,312 --> 00:01:46,250
Resellers, distributors, dropshippers.
They move product they don't own. When

25
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:52,032
inventory belongs to someone else,
underwriting doesn't have assets to back

26
00:01:52,032 --> 00:01:58,361
the float, there's nothing there. When a
dollar goes out to a supplier and doesn't

27
00:01:58,361 --> 00:02:04,533
come back until someone downstream buys
and pays -- that cycle can stretch 30 to

28
00:02:04,533 --> 00:02:05,158
90 days.

29
00:02:05,158 --> 00:02:11,640
Manufacturing -- These companies may have
a cash conversion cycle is often lagging

30
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:17,801
revenue. R&D, tooling, manufacturing
runs, shipping from overseas -- a company

31
00:02:17,801 --> 00:02:24,203
might spend in January on a product that
doesn't generate revenue until May. They

32
00:02:24,203 --> 00:02:29,965
look like DTC brands on the surface, but
their balance sheet looks like a

33
00:02:29,965 --> 00:02:31,165
manufacturer's.

34
00:02:31,165 --> 00:02:36,769
Service providers -- agencies, 3PLs,
staffing companies. The team is on

35
00:02:36,769 --> 00:02:42,933
payroll every two weeks but revenue comes
in on net-30 or net-60 invoices from

36
00:02:42,933 --> 00:02:48,617
clients. There's no inventory to
collateralize and no hard assets on the

37
00:02:48,617 --> 00:02:52,620
balance sheet. Cash goes out fast, comes
back slow.

38
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:58,533
Pre-revenue DTC brands scaling into spend
-- the brand itself might be a perfect

39
00:02:58,533 --> 00:03:04,445
ICP fit, but if they're burning cash to
scale and haven't hit profitability, the

40
00:03:04,445 --> 00:03:09,534
cash conversion cycle is negative.
They're spending on ads today with

41
00:03:09,534 --> 00:03:12,079
revenue that hasn't caught up yet.

42
00:03:12,079 --> 00:03:16,643
None of these are automatic
disqualifications. Net-1 may still be the

43
00:03:16,643 --> 00:03:21,879
right offer. But if you're hearing these
signals on a discovery call, flag them

44
00:03:21,879 --> 00:03:26,645
early — and set the right expectations
before the prospect fills out the

45
00:03:26,645 --> 00:03:27,450
application.
